States</article-title><source>Cancer Causes Control</source><year>2004</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>387</fpage><lpage>397</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Causes Control||15|387||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15141139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guizzetti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bordi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Dieguez-Acuna</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Vitalone</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Madia</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Woods</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Costa</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nuclear factor kappaB activation by muscarinic receptors in astroglial cells: effect of ethanol</article-title><source>Neuroscience</source><year>2003</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>941</fpage><lpage>950</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Neuroscience||120|941||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12927200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammond</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking and death rates: report on forty-four months of follow-up of 187, 783 men. 2. Death rates by cause</article-title><source>J Am Med Assoc</source><year>1958</year><volume>166</volume><fpage>1294</fpage><lpage>1308</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Am Med Assoc||166|1294||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hinz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Loser</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathas</surna